.TH XPRISMCTL 1 "November 2026" "xprism-control 26.11.01"
.SH NAME
xprismctl \- XPrism's settings from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xprismctl
[\fB\-d\fP \fIdisplay\fP] \fIcommand\fP [\fIargs\fP...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xprismctl
shows and changes the runtime settings of the XPrism X server: the
colour settings of each output, the namespaces applications are confined
to, what each namespace may do, and permission prompts.
.PP
Changes last until the server exits. To keep them, put them in
.BR xorg.conf (5)
(HDR, EDR, WideGamut) or in the server's namespace configuration file.
.PP
Namespaces, apps and prompts use the X-NAMESPACE extension, which XPrism
offers only to clients of the session (the root namespace), i.e. with the
session's
.BR $XAUTHORITY .
Confined applications cannot use them.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
The server, its version, and whether the compositor, colour management
and namespaces are available.
.TP
.B displays
Each output: its mode, the HDR, EDR and wide gamut settings (\- where the
driver has none), and what the compositor shows on it.
.TP
\fBdisplay\fP \fIoutput\fP \fBhdr\fP|\fBedr\fP|\fBwide-gamut\fP \fBon\fP|\fBoff\fP
Change a setting of an output.
.TP
.B apps
Connected applications: their namespace, application id or command, process
id, and the permissions they hold.
.TP
.B namespaces
Each namespace, how many applications it has, and its permissions.
.TP
\fBnamespace create\fP \fIname\fP [\fIcap\fP...] [\fB\-\-transient\fP]
Create a namespace, optionally with permissions. A transient one goes
away with its last application.
.TP
\fBnamespace delete\fP \fIname\fP [\fB\-\-close\-apps\fP]
Delete a namespace. Without \fB\-\-close\-apps\fP it fails while
applications use it.
.TP
\fBgrant\fP \fInamespace\fP \fIcap\fP...
.TQ
\fBrevoke\fP \fInamespace\fP \fIcap\fP...
Add or remove permissions; \fBall\fP stands for every one. The
built-in namespaces root and anon cannot be changed.
.TP
.B caps
List the permissions and what each allows.
.TP
.B agent
Answer permission prompts in the terminal: when a confined application
needs a permission it lacks (capability mode enforce), print what it wants
and read an answer: \fBa\fP allow once, \fBw\fP allow while it runs,
\fBd\fP deny, \fBf\fP deny and do not ask again. Only one program answers
prompts at a time.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the server refused or is unreachable, 2 for bad usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
xprismctl display eDP-1 edr on
xprismctl namespace create browser clipboard.read clipboard.write
xprismctl revoke browser clipboard.read
xprismctl namespace delete browser \-\-close\-apps
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xprism\-control\-panel (1),
.BR Xserver (1),
.BR xprism\-permission\-agent (1)
